#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Poll Stoxkart market quotes over REST into the Redis hash `stoxkart:quotes:live`, and keep polling until stopped.

    bin/stoxkart/quotes                              # instruments from the Redis set stoxkart:quotes:subscriptions
    bin/stoxkart/quotes --tokens NSE:760946,MCX:565899
    bin/stoxkart/quotes --interval 2 --requests-per-second 5

    redis-cli SADD stoxkart:quotes:subscriptions NSE:760946 MCX:565899
    redis-cli HGET stoxkart:quotes:live NSE:KWIL
    redis-cli HGETALL stoxkart:quotes:instruments

**Why REST and not a websocket.** Stoxkart documents a binary quote websocket at `ws://inmob.stoxkart.com:7763`. On 2026-09-15 that port refused connections, and the same host on port 443 answered the websocket handshake with HTTP 503 from an AWS load balancer with nothing behind it, so the documented feed cannot be reached. Stoxkart's `POST https://openapi.stoxkart.com/quotes` answers with a full quote, including five levels of depth, for up to 50 instruments of one exchange in about 110 ms, and this script polls it instead. Each tick therefore arrives up to `--interval` seconds after the trade it describes.

**Instruments** are `--tokens` when given, otherwise the members of the Redis set `stoxkart:quotes:subscriptions`. Each is `EXCHANGE:TOKEN`, the field format of `stoxkart:instruments:master`, where the exchange is one of `NSE`, `BSE`, `NFO`, `BFO`, `NSECD`, `BSECD`, `MCX` or `NCDEX`. `BSECD` and `NCDEX` are in Stoxkart's list of exchanges but were refused as invalid on 2026-09-15. Each instrument is named from `stoxkart:instruments:master`: a future or option by its `symbol_description` when that begins with its `symbol` (`NFO:NIFTY26SEPFUT`), a commodity contract, whose description is only the commodity's name, by its symbol, expiry, strike and option type (`MCX:CRUDEOIL21SEP26FUT`), and anything else by its `symbol` (`NSE:KWIL`).

**Polling.** Every cycle asks for every instrument, grouped by exchange in requests of up to 50 tokens, then waits until `--interval` seconds have passed since the cycle began. Requests are spaced so that no more than `--requests-per-second` are sent, below Stoxkart's documented limit of 10 quote requests a second. A quote identical to the previous one for the same instrument is not written again, so a quiet instrument does not fill the stream. The number of ticks written is logged once a minute rather than every cycle. An unknown token comes back as a row with no `token` field, and it is skipped.

**Keys.**

- `stoxkart:quotes:live`, a hash of the latest tick per instrument as JSON, keyed by the instrument's name, such as `NSE:KWIL`, or by `EXCHANGE:TOKEN` when the master does not name it. It is not cleared at startup.
- `stoxkart:quotes:instruments`, a hash of every subscribed `EXCHANGE:TOKEN` to its name, or to an empty string when unnamed. Replaced whole at startup.
- `stoxkart:quotes:stream`, a Redis Stream with every changed tick in arrival order as a `tick` field, which `bin/stoxkart/persist_ticks` writes to `stoxkart.ticks`. Capped at about 100,000 entries.

**The tick.**

| field | from Stoxkart |
| --- | --- |
| `id` | the instrument's name, or `EXCHANGE:TOKEN` |
| `broker`, `mode` | `stoxkart`, `full` |
| `instrument_token`, `exchange` | `EXCHANGE:TOKEN` as subscribed, `exchange` |
| `last_price`, `last_quantity`, `average_price`, `volume` | `last_trade_price`, `last_trade_quantity`, `average_price`, `volume` |
| `buy_quantity`, `sell_quantity` | null, because Stoxkart's `buy_quantity` and `sell_quantity` are the best bid and ask sizes, not the totals |
| `ohlc` | `ohlc.open`, `ohlc.high`, `ohlc.low`, `ohlc.close` |
| `change` | `percent_change` |
| `oi` | `open_interest` |
| `oi_day_high`, `oi_day_low`, `exchange_timestamp` | null, because Stoxkart does not send them |
| `last_trade_time` | `last_trade_time` plus 315532800, because Stoxkart counts seconds from 1980-01-01 UTC; null when it is 0 |
| `depth` | `depth.buy` and `depth.sell`, five levels of `price`, `quantity` and `orders` each |
| `received_at` | when this script received the answer |

Measured against Zerodha's ticks received in the same second on 2026-09-15: `close` is the previous session's close (TCS 2200.80, HDFCBANK 708.25, CRUDEOIL SEP 9717), NSE volume matched exactly, MCX volume and open interest are lots exactly as at Zerodha (CRUDEOIL SEP 6385 and 15677), and the last trade time matched Zerodha's to the second. Stoxkart sends prices as rupee strings, so no divisor is applied.

**Sessions.** A request Stoxkart refuses with `AuthorizationError` logs in again through `StoxkartAPI` before the next request. Any other failed request is logged, and the cycle carries on with the next group.

Exits 0 when stopped with Ctrl+C or SIGTERM, 1 when a login fails, and 2 when there is nothing to subscribe to, an instrument is not `EXCHANGE:TOKEN`, or an option is out of range. Reads only - it places no orders.
"""

